{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2urH2qF5jt2fYoitv6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `jsonpatch/core.py` and added `tests/test_core.py`. All 70 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest tests/test_core.py`). Nothing is committed.\n\n**What's in place**\n\n- **`resolve_pointer`** handles RFC 6901 with `~1` unescaped before `~0`. Invalid pointers raise `PointerError`, including leading zeros, `-` as a read index, out-of-range indexes, and bad `~` escapes.\n- **`apply_patch`** supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test`. It runs on a deep copy, so any failure leaves the input unchanged. On success, `in_place=True` mutates the input.\n- **`test`** uses the spec's equality rules: numbers compare by value, and `True` never equals `1`.\n- Malformed patches (non-list patch, non-dict operation, unknown `op`, missing or mistyped fields) raise `PatchError`.\n\n**Judgment calls the spec didn't settle**\n\n- Removing the document root (`remove` with path `\"\"`) raises `PatchError`.\n- `move` to the same path is a no-op. A `move` whose target is inside its source raises an error.\n- With `in_place=True`, a root that changes type (for example, a dict replaced by a list) can't be mutated into the new type. The function returns the new value and leaves the caller's object alone.\n- `in_place=True` on a container root clears and refills the original container, so the caller's reference sees the result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5393,"cache_read_input_tokens":45174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5393},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e15b914-a1e8-4745-8a28-5027e32d9089","uuid":"f05ea